Dear Quality Assurance Team,

We are submitting an urgent customer quality complaint regarding Amoxicillin Trihydrate 500mg FDF Capsules received at St. Jude Regional Hospital Central Inpatient Pharmacy under Purchase Order #PO-99412.

Key Product & Batch Identifiers:
- Product Name: Amoxicillin Trihydrate Capsules 500mg (FDF)
- Product Strength / Grade: 500mg Oral Capsule (USP / BP Grade)
- Batch / Lot Number: AMX-2024-089A
- Manufacturing Date: 2024-03-15
- Expiration Date: 2026-03-14
- Originating Manufacturing Site: Sterile FDF Formulation Block C
- Affected Quantity: 2,500 units (50 cartons containing 10 blister strips each, approx. 15 kg total pack weight)
- Primary Packaging Material: PVC/PVDC Blister foil backing with aluminum push-through

Defect Description:
During morning dispensing on September 11, 2024, our pharmacy technician noted visible yellow-brown discoloration and distinct mottled speckling on the white capsule shells of Lot AMX-2024-089A upon peeling the blister cavities. Furthermore, micro-pinhole perforations were detected along the heat-seal seam of the blister packaging, suggesting potential moisture ingress during transit or defective sealing parameters.

Immediate Actions Taken:
All 50 cartons from Batch AMX-2024-089A have been immediately placed into pharmacy quarantine (Location: Bio-Vault Quarantine Rack Q-4). No adverse clinical events or patient administration have been reported to date.

Requested QMS Action:
Please initiate an official QMS customer complaint investigation, provide a formal Root Cause Analysis (RCA), and issue a Corrective and Preventive Action (CAPA) plan along with return merchandise authorization (RMA).

